.TH proc_pid 5 "April, 2026"

.SH NAME
.IR /proc/ pid /
\- process information

.SH DESCRIPTION
For each process, a directory entry of this form is available from
.IR proc (5)
with its own files describing the process state. These files include:

.TP
.IR /proc/ pid /cmdline
The commmand line arguments for the process. Arguments are separated by
a \fIrecord separator\fP \- that is, U+1E or 036 octal.

.TP
.IR /proc/ pid /status
A listing of information about the process. Each piece of information
consists of a label, a colon, a space, and then the information string
in various formats.

.TP
.IR /proc/ pid /maps
A listing of memory mapping segments.
Each line indicates a contiguous range with the same properties and
shows the start and end addresses, permissions, file offset, device,
inode number, and file name of mapped files.

.TP
.IR /proc/ pid /exe
Dynamic symbolic link to the main binary of the process.

.TP
.IR /proc/ pid /cwd
Dynamic symbolic link to the current working directory of the process or thread.

.TP
.IR /proc/ pid /fd
Directory containing symbolic links for each open file descriptor, 

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR proc (5)
